// The process and its environment (M6 Task 10).
//
// `exit(code)`, `getenv(name)`, and `getcwd()` are builtins, in scope in every
// file. This module adds the statement-shaped exit a report wants and documents
// the environment and directory spellings beside it.
//
// `getcwd()` answers the current working directory as a fresh owned string. It
// is UTF-8 on every target, including Windows. On failure it answers the empty
// string, matching `read_file` and `getenv` until builtin `Result` lands in R2;
// a real working directory is never empty, so the two cases are distinguishable
// in practice even though the signature cannot say so.
//
// Ownership: `exit_with` never returns and owns nothing. `getcwd()`'s result is
// owned by the caller and released like any other string.
